Create the file test/fixtures/users.ts (relative to the working directory). It must export a named constant `users` of type `User[]` containing exactly 20 realistic User objects.

The User interface is in src/models/user.ts:
```ts
export interface User {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

Requirements:
- Import with a relative path and no extension, matching test/strings.test.ts style: `import type { User } from "../../src/models/user";`
- Use double quotes, 2-space indentation, semicolons.
- `id`: unique UUID v4-format strings (hard-coded literals, all distinct).
- `name`: diverse realistic full names; `email`: unique, lowercase, derived from the name, using example.com / example.org / example.net domains only.
- `createdAt` / `updatedAt`: `new Date("...Z")` ISO literals in 2023–2025; updatedAt must be >= createdAt for every entry.
- No randomness, no faker, no new dependencies, no other files changed.

Done when `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` passes with no errors.

